.TH VOLVOX 1 "July 2026" "Volvox" "Volvox Compiler / Interpreter Manual"
.SH NAME
volvox \- Volvox compiler and interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B volvox
[
.I options
]
[
.I file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B volvox
is the compiler and interpreter for the Volvox programming language.
It can compile Volvox source files (.vx) to native executables,
object files, or LLVM IR, and can also JIT-compile and run programs
directly.
.PP
The following assumes that the
.B volvox
executable is located in a directory that is included in the
.B PATH
environment variable. Otherwise, specify the full path (e.g.
.BR bin/volvox
or
.BR /my/path/bin/volvox ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Print a help summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Be verbose. Show configuration information and invocations of external
tools such as the system compiler or linker.
.TP
.B \-V
Show Volvox version and platform information and exit.
.TP
.B \-c
Compile only; do not link. Unless
.B \-o
is given, the result of compiling
.I filename.vx
will be an object file named
.IR filename.o
(or
.IR filename.obj
on Windows). Statements outside of defined functions will be placed in
a function called
.BR main ,
unless
.B \-M
is given.
.TP
.B \-g
Create debug information for use with debuggers such as
.BR lldb
or
.BR gdb .
Currently debug information is only created for fixed-size objects
(basic types, structs, and fixed-size arrays). Dynamic objects may
require special support in the debugger.
.PP
On Windows, only the
.B mingw
target is supported. Thread-local
.B global
variables are not visible in the debugger (this is not specific to
Volvox).
.TP
.B \-r
Compile the program and run it immediately. Consider
.B \-j
instead for JIT compilation.
.TP
.B \-j
JIT-compile and run the program.
.TP
.B \-J
JIT-compile and run statement by statement, as if entered interactively.
This is significantly slower than
.BR \-j ,
but leaves a prompt to enter further commands (unless the last statement
was
.B return
or
.BR exit ).
.TP
.BI \-d ", " \-D
Dump intermediate LLVM IR code at different stages. Only useful to
debug the Volvox compiler itself. Consider
.B \-emit-llvm
instead for producing a usable IR file.
.TP
.B \-M mainfn
Use
.IR mainfn
as the function name for statements outside of function definitions
(default:
.BR main ).
Useful in combination with
.B \-c
when manual linking is done.
.TP
.B \-f<flag>
Enable a compilation flag. The following flags are supported:
.RS 4
.TP
.B \-fPIC
Generate position-independent code suitable for creating a shared
object file (.so.*).
.TP
.B \-fdiv-floored
Signed integer division is floored; the remainder gets the sign of the
divisor. This is the default in Volvox. Example:
.br
.RB \-13 " / " 4
\(en> \-4
.br
.RB \-13 " % " 4
\(en> 3
.br
.RB 13 " / " \-4
\(en> \-4
.br
.RB 13 " % " \-4
\(en> \-3
.TP
.B \-fdiv-c99
Signed division rounds toward zero; the remainder gets the sign of the
dividend. This is the default in C99 and later (C89 behaviour was
undefined). Example:
.br
.RB \-13 " / " 4
\(en> \-3
.br
.RB \-13 " % " 4
\(en> \-1
.br
.RB 13 " / " \-4
\(en> \-3
.br
.RB 13 " % " \-4
\(en> 1
.PP
In both modes (\-fdiv-floored and \-fdiv-c99) the following equation
always holds:
.IR "a=b*(a/b)+(a%b)"
In practice, integer divisions should not involve negative numbers to
avoid confusion.
.TP
.B \-fno-index-checks, \-fno-idx-chk
Do not check array indices to be within the allowed range.
(Note: these checks are not implemented yet.)
.TP
.B \-fpres, \-fprint-results
Print the result of each expression outside of functions. This is the
default in interactive JIT mode and when
.B \-J
is given.
.TP
.B \-fno-pres, \-fno-print-results
Do not print the result of each expression outside of functions.
This is the default when
.B \-j
is given and when compiling to a binary object file or executable.
.RE
.TP
.B \-emit-llvm
Create a file
.I name.ll
that contains LLVM's intermediate representation.
.TP
.B \-On[m]
Optimize with level
.IR n .
If
.I m
is also given, use
.IR n
as the optimization level for the intermediate representation and
.I m
for the generation of binary machine code. The default is
.B \-O2
for normal compilation and
.B \-O0
when debug information is added (\-g).
.TP
.B \-i file
Include
.I file
before parsing the main program.
.TP
.B \-o file
Use
.I file
as the output file. This option is mandatory if more than one input
file is given.
.TP
.B \-strip
Strip unneeded symbols from the resulting executable to produce a
smaller file.
.TP
.B \-s
.IR size
Set the stack size per thread. The value may contain
.BR kB ,
.BR MB ,
or
.B GB
suffix (default: 10MB). Mostly relevant on Windows.
.TP
.B \-m<target>
Specify the target system. Currently only relevant on Windows.
Possible values are:
.RS 4
.TP
.B \-mingw
Create a MINGW binary (this is the default).
.TP
.B \-msvc
Create a Microsoft Visual C binary. This requires that Microsoft
Visual Studio is installed.
.RE
.TP
.B \-no\-<flag>
Disable a feature. Supported flags:
.RS 4
.TP
.B \-no-lto
Do not perform link-time optimization. (Default: no LTO when
.B \-g
is given, thin-LTO otherwise.)
.TP
.B \-no-setup-con
Do not inject code to set up the console for color output.
.RE
.TP
.B \-t
Run test cases. Test cases are functions whose name starts with
.BR test_ ,
that have no arguments, and that return
.BR bool .
.TP
.B \-C<n>,<g>,<b>
Set ANSI-256 colors for line number, greater sign, and background of
the interactive prompt (default: 30,100,236).
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I file ...
One or more input files with extension
.B .vx
containing the Volvox program source code.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B non-zero
An error occurred (e.g., compilation error, runtime error). In JIT mode
the number passed to
.IR exit
or final
.IR return \.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Compile and link one source file to an executable:
.IP
.B volvox myprogram.vx
.TP
Compile and link several source files to an executable:
.IP
.B volvox \-o myprogram source1.vx source2.vx
.TP
Compile only (no linking):
.IP
.B volvox \-c myprogram.vx
.TP
JIT-compile and run:
.IP
.B volvox \-j myprogram.vx
.TP
Interactive JIT mode:
.IP
.B volvox
.TP
Compile with debug information:
.IP
.B volvox \-g myprogram.vx
.TP
Generate LLVM IR:
.IP
.B volvox \-emit-llvm myprogram.vx
.SH BUGS
Array index checking is not yet implemented, despite the
.B \-fno-index-checks
flag being documented. There are many other bugs as this project
is in pre alpha stage. 
.SH AUTHOR
Developed by the Volvox project.
